  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "How to read this diagram",
      "items": [
        "Each box is a part of the system; colour = what kind (see the legend top-right).",
        "An arrow means 'talks to'; dashed = background/optional. Click a box's SRC badge to see the code."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "orange",
      "title": "Complete code map (every module)",
      "items": [
        "app/pipeline.py - the cascade that ties STT, the dialogue manager and TTS together.",
        "app/stt/ - speech-to-text engines (a stub and a Whisper backend) behind one interface.",
        "app/tts/ - text-to-speech engines (a stub and pyttsx3) behind one interface.",
        "app/dialogue/ - the dialogue manager (slot filling), NLU (intent + slots) and an optional LLM NLU.",
        "app/booking/ - the booking store (SQLite or in-memory) behind one interface.",
        "app/audio/ - microphone input and barge-in (interrupt) handling.",
        "app/state/ - per-call session state.",
        "app/events.py - the normalized event bus behind the live timeline.",
        "app/main.py - the FastAPI app: turn endpoints + the browser console."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Guided tour - one turn",
      "items": [
        "1. A caller sends voice or text to the FastAPI app (or uses the console).",
        "2. The pipeline runs STT to get a transcript.",
        "3. The dialogue manager fills slots using NLU (optionally an LLM) and the booking store.",
        "4. TTS speaks the reply; session state is kept per call; events feed the live timeline."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Why it is built this way",
      "items": [
        "Cascaded STT->LLM/NLU->TTS: each stage is swappable and separately testable (stubs run with no models).",
        "The dialogue manager owns slot filling, so the model is not trusted to track booking state.",
        "Barge-in lets a caller interrupt, so the agent stops speaking and listens."
      ]
    }
  ]
